    {
      "type": "Text",
      "props": {
        "id": "Text-f8336ec7-222d-42f8-a7a8-8b392bcb62e9",
        "text": "<p>Kapaas is a collection of surfaces developed as a part of a classroom project. Right before the project began, I had visited a cotton farm. The field looked very light, soft and delicate from a distance, but as soon as I stepped in, I realized how the soft cotton bolls are protected and held by the rough, hard pods. The fragile cotton bolls push themselves out of their protecting layers to come out and bloom. This experience made me choose cotton as my inspiration for this project.</p>",
        "style": "body",
        "align": "start",
        "measure": "normal",
        "layout": {
          "width": "text",
          "space": "s",
          "show": "all",
          "motion": "none"
        }
      }
    },
